        {
            "id": "pages_daily_landing",
            "display_name": "Entry Pages Daily Report (limited ranking)",
            "_comment": "Epic 10 story 10.3: entry pages = sessions by GA4 landingPage. Story 10.3 Task 1 design decision: landingPage and pagePath are DISTINCT GA4 dimensions; a single runReport with BOTH produces a landingPage x pagePath cross-join (cardinality explosion). Entry pages and top pages are two independent marginal top-N lists with NO join needed (unlike GSC query>page in 10.5). So TWO report profiles, each a single-dimension top-N runReport. This profile: sessions by landingPage, orderBys sessions DESC + limit=page_top_n. row_limit is the page_top_n bound (default 50, bounded 10..200). verification_expected_rows_per_day <= 1 metric-carrier x N (upper bound, NOT exact: the long tail beyond N is dropped by design).",
            "metrics": [
                "sessions"
            ],
            "dimensions": [
                "date",
                "landing_page"
            ],
            "extraction_capabilities": {
                "row_limit": 50,
                "row_limit_min": 10,
                "row_limit_max": 200,
                "filters_supported": true,
                "realtime": false
            },
            "extraction_path": "custom_pull",
            "verification_expected_rows_per_day": 50
        },
        {
            "id": "pages_daily_paths",
            "display_name": "Top Pages Daily Report (limited ranking)",
            "_comment": "Epic 10 story 10.3: most-viewed pages = screen_page_views by GA4 pagePath. Second of the two page profiles (see pages_daily_landing _comment for the cross-join rationale). AI-53 honesty: the screenPageViews metric name is DECLARED per the api-schema but NOT verified live (no GA4 property connected). AC 11 / AI-13 confirms the exact metric name at the first live pass (Phase B gate); fallback if absent is sessions by pagePath (confirmed). row_limit is the page_top_n bound (default 50, bounded 10..200). verification_expected_rows_per_day <= 1 metric-carrier x N (upper bound; long tail beyond N dropped by design).",
            "metrics": [
                "screen_page_views"
