                "row_limit_max": 200,
                "filters_supported": true,
                "realtime": false
            },
            "extraction_path": "custom_pull",
            "verification_expected_rows_per_day": 50
        },
        {
            "id": "acquisition_daily_session",
            "display_name": "Acquisition Daily Report - Last Click (limited ranking)",
            "_comment": "Epic 16 story 16.1: last-click attribution = conversions + sessions by GA4 sessionSourceMedium x sessionCampaignName. AI-53 honesty: the sessionSourceMedium / sessionCampaignName dimension names are DECLARED per the GA4 Data API doc but NOT verified live (no GA4 property connected). AC11 / AI-13 confirms the exact dimension names via the properties/{p}/metadata endpoint at the first live pass (Phase B gate). This profile carries BOTH acquisition dimensions on the same runReport row (GA4 returns them jointly for the last-click axis); the mart derives TWO MARGINAL partitions (session_source_medium, session_campaign) from it -- this is NOT a cross-join between attribution axes (the forbidden cross-join is session x first-user). Separate runReport from acquisition_daily_first_user (two marginal pulls, 10.3 pattern). dimensions lead with 'date' (manifest contract). row_limit is the top-N bound (default 50, clamped 10..200 via _get_page_top_n); orderBys conversions DESC + limit=top_n. Long tail beyond N dropped by design. verification_expected_rows_per_day <= top_n (upper bound, NOT exact). Conversion-event filter (lead_event_name) is a project preference, NOT hardcoded -- BLOCKED Phase B (default = all conversions).",
            "metrics": [
                "conversions",
                "sessions"
            ],
            "dimensions": [
                "date",
                "session_source_medium",
                "session_campaign"
            ],
            "extraction_capabilities": {
                "row_limit": 50,
                "row_limit_min": 10,
                "row_limit_max": 200,
                "filters_supported": true,
                "realtime": false
            },
            "extraction_path": "custom_pull",
            "verification_expected_rows_per_day": 50
        },
        {
            "id": "acquisition_daily_first_user",
            "display_name": "Acquisition Daily Report - First Click (limited ranking)",
            "_comment": "Epic 16 story 16.1: first-click attribution = conversions by GA4 firstUserSourceMedium. AI-53 honesty: firstUserSourceMedium is DECLARED per the GA4 Data API doc but NOT verified live (Phase B gate, AC11 / AI-13 confirms via metadata). Separate runReport from acquisition_daily_session (combining session x first-user dimensions in ONE runReport would produce a session x first-user cross-join -- cardinality explosion + semantic nonsense). dimensions lead with 'date'. row_limit is the top-N bound (default 50, clamped 10..200); orderBys conversions DESC + limit=top_n; long tail dropped by design. verification_expected_rows_per_day <= top_n (upper bound). Conversion-event filter (lead_event_name) BLOCKED Phase B (default = all conversions).",
            "metrics": [
